# Findings the release scan deliberately does not block on. Every entry needs a reason and a way out; review when you bump Spring Boot.

# spring-webmvc 6.2.19 is the newest 6.2.x release; Trivy lists the fix only in Spring Framework 7 (Spring Boot 4), a major upgrade
# that needs its own change. Exit: migrate to Spring Boot 4 (tracked in docs/adr).
CVE-2026-47884
CVE-2026-47890
# spring-webflux (api-gateway) has the same Spring Framework 7-only fix
CVE-2026-47892

# Go standard library (1.27.1) inside the base image's /usr/bin/pebble (the image's init process), not code we build; we never expose
# it to network input. Exit: rebuild on a
# base image whose pebble is built with Go >= 1.27.3 (rebuilding the image picks it up automatically once published).
CVE-2026-111943
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-97031
